          "path": "_m/g/f/m/0/fearn-abbey-wp/fearn-abbey-and-parish-church-.jpg",
          "filename": "Fearn Abbey and Parish Church - geograph.org.uk - 42137.jpg",
          "caption": "Fearn Abbey and Parish Church. The Abbey was built here in 1238 and rebuilt in the mid 1300s. Converted to a Parish Church when  the   reformation came to the area in 1560. Hit by lightning on Sunday the 10 Aug 1742 the heavy roof collapsed on the congregation and killed around 50 people. The building was abandoned and a new Church built but by the 1770s it too was in ruins. The old original 1300s building was then rebuilt with stone from the new Church and put back in use.",
          "alt": "Fearn Abbey and Parish Church. The Abbey was built here in 1238 and rebuilt in the mid 1300s. Converted to a Parish Church when  the   reformation came to the area in 1560. Hit by lightning on Sunday the 10 Aug 1742 the heavy roof collapsed on the congregation and killed around 50 people. The building was abandoned and a new Church built but by the 1770s it too was in ruins. The old original 1300s building was then rebuilt with stone from the new Church and put back in use.",
          "width": 640,
          "height": 439,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
          "artist": "Jim Bain",
